⟦ class_tree_classify | CLASS-TREE-CLASSIFY-v2 | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-08-19 ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status active
// design: docs/design/sources/plugin-class-taxonomy-v1/plugin_class_taxonomy.vsm
// (PLUGIN-CLASS-TAXONOMY-v1 — árbol de la clase CLASSIFY; R16_impl_with_design)
// .opencode/plugins/trees/classify.tree.vsm — socratic tree of class CLASSIFY
// (PLUGIN-CLASS-TAXONOMY-v1, design-sources/plugin-class-taxonomy-v1).
//
// v2 (2026-08-19, HOOK-ARGS-CONTRACT-REPAIR): the v1 tree only knew 5
// prefixes (VSL-LANG-, THEORY-VC-, THEORY-AP-, BOOT-, S5-) while the real
// taxonomy has ~157 types (DIR, VSL, EXP, THEORY, LEARNING, VSF, S5, S1,
// AGENT...). Result: 256/279 .vsm docs did NOT match → certified=False →
// the CLASSIFY plugin shouted "opina sin certificar (R10)" on every write
// even after the args-contract fix. v2 covers the real taxonomy by mapping
// the dominant prefixes to their real homes under docs/spec_revision/.
//
// R10: every predicate here is a DETERMINISTIC builtin (certified=True) —
// structural evidence, never LLM opinion.
// R9: ctx_has guard — if the context lacks the TYPE (unreadable doc), the
// root answers UNKNOWN → the shell reports '?' visible, never the silent
// else_home. UNKNOWN is not FALSE.
//
// Write-time universal (fase c): the SAME tree is what the write-time gate
// evaluates when a doc is saved — the questionnaire IS the gate.
//
// R10-CLASSIFY-FIX (2026-08-19): PLUGIN-* catch-all → home="design" —
// SPECS of plugins live in design-sources/ and sandbox/, NOT
// .opencode/plugins/. Implemented plugins are .ts files (vsf-*.ts) without
// a TYPE=PLUGIN-* header. The old home="plugin" actively BLOCKED writing
// design specs through the per-file socratic-classify gate (confirmed via
// R18 log line 1653 result=fail + user-captured red message; task
// CLASSIFY-PATH-NULL-NOISE-2026-08-19). PLUGIN-S2-COORDINATION- maps to
// sandbox (its current home); the catch-all falls to design.
//
// R10-CLASSIFY-FIX-2 (2026-08-20): CODEBASE-ECOSYSTEM-* / STUDY-* →
// home="internal" — informes de estudio/auditoría internos del agente en
// docs/internal/ (2a faceta de CLASSIFY-PATH-NULL-NOISE: el TYPE
// CODEBASE-ECOSYSTEM-STUDY-FASE-0 caía a else_home=system → falso
// 'fuera de lugar' sobre docs/internal/).

socratic("CLASS-TREE-CLASSIFY") = {
  op: AND,
  children: [
    { predicate: "ctx_has", args: ["$ctx", "type"] },
    {
      op: OR,
      children: [
        { predicate: "type_prefix", args: ["$type", "VSL-WORKLIST-"], home: "ledger" },
        { predicate: "type_prefix", args: ["$type", "VSL-LANGUAGE-PRIMER-"], home: "boot" },
        { predicate: "type_prefix", args: ["$type", "VSL-LANG-"], home: "vsl-language" },
        { predicate: "type_prefix", args: ["$type", "VSL-LANGUAGE-"], home: "vsl-language" },
        { predicate: "type_prefix", args: ["$type", "VSL-CORE-BOOT-"], home: "boot" },
        { predicate: "type_prefix", args: ["$type", "VSL-HARD-RULES-"], home: "boot" },
        { predicate: "type_prefix", args: ["$type", "VSL-AGENT-ONBOARDING-"], home: "boot" },
        { predicate: "type_prefix", args: ["$type", "VSL-REGULATION-LAYER-"], home: "boot" },
        { predicate: "type_prefix", args: ["$type", "THEORY-VC-"], home: "s3-control" },
        { predicate: "type_prefix", args: ["$type", "THEORY-AP-"], home: "s4-intelligence" },
        { predicate: "type_prefix", args: ["$type", "THEORY-CL-"], home: "archive" },
